      feat(c-sharp): allow lenient escape sequences in string literals
      
      Override `escape_sequence` to accept any `\<char>` after the spec
      escapes have had a chance to match. Roslyn rejects unrecognized escape
      sequences (CS1009), but semgrep is a static analyzer that wants to
      scan real-world code that occasionally contains these (e.g. Windows
      paths embedded in regular string literals: `"\\share\images"`). With
      the upstream grammar's strict pattern, tree-sitter emits an ERROR node
      and semgrep's parse-error gate fails the file entirely.
      
      `./test-lang c-sharp` stays green: 199/199 corpus tests pass and
      ConvexHull.cs continues to parse cleanly.
